ngs from the Opus review, and allow shared x on scatter\n212d2c8 Status: every pipeline module reviewed; four fix runs and chart core part 1 in progress\ne85a2d0 Review of view and scene by Opus 5.5 xhigh recorded (1 blocking, 10 major, 6 minor); contracts gain a donut color index and a bar pattern\n03b94b9 Review of lookup, reader and messages by Opus 5.5 xhigh recorded (1 blocking, 4 major, 10 minor); contracts updated\n01c3e19 Layout and simplification: fix the 14 findings from the Opus review\n641ac6a Review of renderers and theme by Codex gpt-6.2-astra xhigh recorded (2 blocking, 12 major, 4 minor)\n1c65840 Review of the data layer by Opus 5.5 xhigh recorded (2 blocking, 10 major, 6 minor); registry gains AX134 and AX152, AX105 gets a cap\naf7f3d5 Status: all pipeline modules in; chart core part 1 dispatched; four cross-reviews running\n953deae Lookup: scatter references carry their x position (contract change); tests and eviction handling follow with the review fixes\n4527458 Build writes the standalone stylesheet from the library's CSS string\n34c819d View and scene building for all five chart types (Codex gpt-6.2-sol xhigh); review pending\n5f9f094 Lookup, reader model and built-in messages (Codex gpt-6.2-sol xhigh); review by Opus pending\ndf6d993 Review of layout and simplification by Opus 5.5 xhigh recorded (1 blocking, 4 major, 9 minor); F5 wording reconciled with the join rule\n4055be2 Scales and formatting: fix the 14 defects from the cross-provider review\n9348d7c Status: round 2 dispatched (view and scene, lookup and reader); reviews of data and layout running\n3940ef5 Data layer and diagnostics (Codex gpt-6.2-sol xhigh); review by Opus pending\nd9154f4 Spec F6 wording made exact; review of scales package recorded (2 blocking, 12 major findings, fixes in progress)\nf7bbbc0 Layout with label fitting, and drawing simplification (Codex gpt-6.2-sol xhigh); review by Opus pending\n759032a Benchmark harness, first version (Opus 5.5 high)\n3e61e01 Scales, ticks, time zones and formatting (Opus 5.5 high); review by Codex gpt-6.2-astra pending\nfec5701 Status: round 1 work packages dispatched\n2047383 Contracts revision after review: stable datum refs, donut and scatter views, signed stacks, shared projection, diagnostic effects\n49f0029 M0: workspace, toolchain, internal contracts, test and build scaffolding\n2d5fb4f Design documents (revision 3), Phase 1 research and review records\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
