{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'head -60 acceptance/report.md && tail -12 acceptance/report.md && head -60 bench/size-latest.json && tail -35 bench/size-latest.json'","aggregated_output":"# Acceptance report\n\nStatic coverage only. No Vitest reports supplied.\n## Warnings\n\nTitles the source scan cannot vouch for, with no run to confirm them (no result of their file and no EVIDENCE.json beside it).\n\n- L2/compact: title not confirmed by any run (it matches a template only) in packages/axylo/test/theme/palette.test.ts: light: 1. every series color reaches 3:1 on the default background\n- L2/compact: title not confirmed by any run (it matches a template only) in packages/axylo/test/theme/palette.test.ts: dark: 1. every series color reaches 3:1 on the default background\n- DX1/line: title not confirmed by any run (it matches a template only) in tests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts: renders under the production condition\n- DX1/line: title not confirmed by any run (it matches a template only) in tests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts: renders under the development condition\n- DX4/line: title not confirmed by any run (it matches a template only) in tests/dist/flavours.browser.test.ts: hints print once, are delivered either way, and warnings print once\n- DX4/line: title not confirmed by any run (it matches a template only) in tests/dist/flavours.browser.test.ts: hints print never, are delivered either way, and warnings print once\n\n## Packed size measurement\n\nMeasured from the pack this tree makes (sha512-LCn3nSF7J5rm…).\n\n- line only (examples/first-chart/npm.ts) · 280,849 minified JS bytes, 96.81 KiB gzipped, 98 KiB target · [bench/size-latest.json](../bench/size-latest.json)\n- everything (export * from axylo) · 334,941 minified JS bytes, 115.74 KiB gzipped, 116 KiB target · [bench/size-latest.json](../bench/size-latest.json)\n- area only (export { area } from axylo) · 286,339 minified JS bytes, 98.72 KiB gzipped · [bench/size-latest.json](../bench/size-latest.json)\n- bar only (export { bar } from axylo) · 281,874 minified JS bytes, 97.20 KiB gzipped · [bench/size-latest.json](../bench/size-latest.json)\n- scatter only (export { scatter } from axylo) · 267,529 minified JS bytes, 92.52 KiB gzipped · [bench/size-latest.json](../bench/size-latest.json)\n- donut only (export { donut } from axylo) · 247,371 minified JS bytes, 84.64 KiB gzipped · [bench/size-latest.json](../bench/size-latest.json)\n- validate only (export { validate } from axylo) · 58,410 minified JS bytes, 20.56 KiB gzipped · [bench/size-latest.json](../bench/size-latest.json)\n- script tag (axylo.iife.min.js + axylo.css) · 335,535 minified JS bytes, 118.87 KiB gzipped · [bench/size-latest.json](../bench/size-latest.json)\n\n\n## Status by chart type\n\n- pass · 6\n- fail · 0\n- weak · 164\n- no evidence · 0\n- not run · 138\n- not recorded for this revision · 0\n- cannot be verified here · 11\n- not applicable · 257\n\nThe matrix contains individual test citations and applicability reasons. [acceptance/matrix.json](matrix.json)\n\n| Criterion | Statement | line | area | bar | scatter | donut | compact |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| L1 | No visible text overlaps other text or is clipped, and no label disappears unannounced. Remedies in order: thin (time, date, numeric and `ordered` category axes only); wrap to at most three lines; rotate up to 45°; truncate in the middle, keeping labels distinct, with the full text in tooltip and table. If labels still do not fit, the note \"Some labels hidden. See table.\" appears and AX143 suggests horizontal bars. The orientation never changes on its own. | weak | weak | weak | weak | weak | not applicable |\n| C4 | With more than one series, compact lines differ by dash as well as colour, and compact bars by fill pattern between neighbours (A5), since there is no legend; AX131 suggests one series per compact chart. | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | weak |\n| F1 | Bar and area value axes always include zero; an author domain that excludes zero is widened to zero and raises AX110. | not applicable | not run | not run | not applicable | not applicable | not run |\n| F2 | Missing values are never drawn as zero and never bridged unless the author asks: an explicit null is a gap, silently; a value isolated between two gaps is a visible point; a missing bar shows a \"no data\" mark at the baseline, distinct from a zero bar, and a slot a series merely has no row for gets no bar and no mark; on a time or date axis with a regular step an absent step is a gap and raises AX105; missing: 'zero' turns absent and null values into zeros for counts; tooltip, table and announcements say \"No data\". | not run | not run | weak | not run | not run | weak |\n| F3 | Input that cannot be plotted as given is reported, never guessed. The registry in section 3.5 fixes each code's level, delivery, what is drawn and what the reader sees: errors and warnings print once per code per page in every build, hints in development builds only; strict: true throws synchronously from create, update and append for errors and warnings found while validating; late findings are reported, never thrown; data findings name the field and the first row indexes in the caller's form. A value formatter that throws (AX160) shows the reader's note, a tick formatter that throws is reported without one; AX199 covers a throw by Axylo or by author code it runs. | weak | weak | weak | weak | weak | weak |\n| F12 | When a warning means values were left out or changed, the chart says so to the reader: a short note (\"Values not shown: 2. See table.\", worded so it reads correctly for any count) inside the figure and in the accessibility tree, in every build. | not run | not run | not run | not run | not run | not applicable |\n| F10 | Stacks place positive and negative values on their own sides of zero, and the axis covers both totals. The readout's total is the sum when every component has the same sign; with mixed signs it gives the positive total and the negative total, not their net. A missing component is drawn with zero height and the stack is marked \"incomplete\" in tooltip, table and announcements. A component is missing whenever its series has no value at that x, a slot it has no row for included (a weekly series stacked with a daily one is incomplete between its rows; owner's decision), and a stacked series' line follows its band. | not applicable | weak | weak | not applicable | not applicable | weak |\n| F8 | Donut slices keep the given order, start at 12 o'clock and run clockwise; the legend shows every slice's value and percentage as text, in slice order. A zero slice is listed without an arc, a null slice as \"No data\". A negative value is AX120 and the chart shows its error state. With more than eight slices that have an arc, the seven largest are drawn and the rest of those are grouped as \"Other (n)\", with AX121; zero and null slices never count toward the limit and are never grouped; the table lists every category. Shares have at most one fraction digit. An all-zero donut shows the empty state. | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | not run | not applicable |\n| F4 | Three temporal types, never mixed silently: calendar dates read the same in every viewer time zone; instants (epoch milliseconds declared time, Date objects, ISO strings with an offset) are shown in timeZone (default the viewer's), with the zone named in the tooltip heading and the description; wall-clock times are shown as written, with AX112; instants all on one time of day, whole days apart, raise AX111; a bare number is never taken for an instant. | not run | not run | not run | not run | not applicable | not run |\n| F11 | Line, area and scatter are drawn in x order whatever the input order; on line, area and bar two rows with the same x in one series are AX108 and that series is not drawn; on scatter, points sharing an x (or both coordinates) are ordinary data. | not run | not run | not run | not run | not applicable | not run |\n| F5 | No smoothing. A line denser than the screen is simplified so that, for every device-pixel column and every contiguous run of valid samples inside it, the stroke covers exactly that run's minimum and maximum; a break between two runs is kept even inside one column; a slot a series merely has no row for (weekly beside daily) does not break its line, except inside a stack (F10); stacked areas are simplified on their cumulative sums; exact values always come from the data, not the drawing. | not run | weak | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | weak |\n| T-dense-line | Simplified drawing when dense · F5 | not run | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable |\n| T-dense-area | Simplified drawing when dense · F5 on cumulative sums | not applicable | weak | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable |\n| T-dense-bar | Simplified drawing when dense · No; more bars than pixels raises a hint | not applicable | not applicable | not run | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable |\n| T-dense-donut | Simplified drawing when dense · No | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | weak | not applicable |\n| T-dense-scatter | Simplified drawing when dense · No in 1.0; above 50,000 points a hint says drawing may be slow | not applicable | not applicable | not applicable | not run | not applicable | not applicable |\n| F7 | On value axes (y of line, area and bar; both axes of scatter) the zoomed view stays inside the author's domain if given, otherwise inside the automatic domain; after a zoom on x, a y axis with no author domain is fitted again to the values in view. A continuous x of line, area or bar spans exactly its data and the x references it draws (plus half a band